From fb4b86b728c08451e9df158c7c10b00837c0161d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:43:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 51/53] civ45: seven faiths founded by tech, spreading on their
 own

Issue 273 (notes/freeciv45/design/religion.md). The first civ to learn
Mysticism, Polytheism, Ruler Apotheosis, Philosophy, Astronomy,
Monotheism or Theology founds one of seven invented faiths in its
largest city, which becomes the holy city. Faiths spread each turn into
nearby cities that follow none, faster near the same owner's cities
and the holy city. Each civ's state faith is the one most of its cities
follow; cities of the state faith get one more content citizen, and
one more each from a Temple and a Cathedral. A holy city adds 2 history
a turn and can build the Shrine (2 content, +25% gold, 1 gold a turn per
city of its faith).

Marker buildings that cannot be built carry the native effects, so the
AI sees them; the Lua record fc45_rel_<city id> is the source of truth
and re-creates markers that are sold, razed or lost at conquest.
---
 data/civ45/buildings.ruleset | 407 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 data/civ45/effects.ruleset   | 229 ++++++++++++++++++++
 data/civ45/script.lua        | 205 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 841 insertions(+)

